<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50362" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱλήκω</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ],
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱλάσκομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be gracious</i>, of a god,
			once in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> in subj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ κεν Ἀπόλλων ἡμῖν ἱλήκῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					21.365
				</span></i>
			; elsewh. in opt., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱλήκοι Ἀπόλλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					165
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱλήκοις, Δέσποινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.72
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Rufin.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱλήκοις, Πολιοῦχε</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				9.154
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοὶ μάκαρες, ἱλήκοιτε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.68
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				8.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.25
			</span></i>. (Prob. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἱλ-</span>, cf.
		sq.)</div>
